WEBVTT

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.720
Nothing beats a cold drink after a hot bath!

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.730
Ryo-chan, you're back?

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.360
Sako-chan.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.490
What?

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.670
We need to talk.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.000
<b><i>Backflip!!</i></b>

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.970
<i>We made it through prefecturals 
with a second place finish.</i>

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:03.510
<i>Now we get to soar together a while longer.</i>

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.730
<i>We still get to soar...</i>

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.730
<b>Certificate of Merit
Second Place</b>

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.870
<i>We get to soar!</i>

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:13.530
Yes!

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.650
Whatcha yesin' about, eh?

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.480
Quit grinning and get working.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.860
R-Right...

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.530
Huh? Onagawa?

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.910
Onagawa-senpai?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.460
Still kicking yourself 
over that mistake yesterday?

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.670
Just practice a little and—

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:30.580
Gosh!

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.840
We took second at prefecturals, 
but still no love from the ladies!

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:35.920
Huh?

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.510
I was hoping for a little more...

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.510
"Second place at prefecturals? 
That's awesome!"

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.640
"Won't you teach me how to do 
men's rhythmic gymnastics?"

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.530
But it's all coming up dry!

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.560
So that's the problem, huh?

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.430
I get it, though.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.880
You do, huh?

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.730
But what can you do?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.580
Morning, everyone.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.780
Coach! And Misato-kun?

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.940
What brings you here at this hour?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.660
He called me late last night.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.830
He said he wants to stay at the dorm.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:07.660
What?!

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.740
Misato-kun at the dorm with us?

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.280
Well, well!

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.380
Can't bear to be without us, huh?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.710
Lonely Little Ace.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.200
Don't call me that.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.840
The prefectural tournament made it clear.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.010
We need significant 
improvement to beat Shiro High.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.770
I really want to go to the Inter-High.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.830
That means we need to get better.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.190
And not just as individuals. As a group!

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:40.520
Okay! Then let's burn even hotter!

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.180
Indeed.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.030
Yeah!

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.030
Yah!

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.490
You don't have to get home, Misato-kun?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:46.990
I will on weekends.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.670
Then the rest is up to you, Captain.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:50.790
Right!

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.060
It oughta go without saying...

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.500
but we've got a chore wheel system 'round here

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.000
for cookin', laundry, and cleanin'.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.130
You're gonna start by showin' us 
what you can do in the kitchen...

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.170
Misato!

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.650
Let's eat!

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.220
So good!

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.030
Even his cleanup is flawless.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.610
What are you now, Perfect Ace?

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.840
Don't call me that.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.190
Well, we've had grub and we got Misato.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:36.990
Time to practice—

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.330
Hold it.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.740
Captain. Everyone.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.490
Aren't we forgetting something?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.930
Prefecturals are over. 
And two weeks from now...

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:46.280
<b>MI</b>

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:46.530
<b>DT</b>

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:46.780
<b>ER</b>

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.090
<b>MS</b>

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.770
It's midterms!

00:04:47.090 --> 00:05:01.110
<b>MIDTERMS</b>

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.690
Oh, crap! Oh, hell!

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.080
I totally forgot!

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.460
I wasn't thinking!

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.710
I haven't studied at all...

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.040
Activities are on hold until afterward.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.110
We need to make good on our promise 
to our coach for another year.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.500
What promise?

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.570
If even one of us receives a failing grade,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:08.630
we're all barred from the 
Sekiou University gym for the year.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:09.990
In other words...

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:10.990
What?!

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.470
We won't be able to use the mat?

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.000
What?

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.210
The captain, Onagawa, 
and Watari always scrape by.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.380
Huh? Then what about you two?

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.300
Not a problem.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.380
What about you, Shotaro?

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:30.470
My English is dicey...

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:32.510
Okay. And you, Misato?

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.800
Did you struggle anywhere in junior high?

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.070
Never.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.050
Great.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.570
You help Shotaro with English, then.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.190
What?

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:43.760
All right! I'll handle 
Shichigahama and Onagawa.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.570
Er, wait...

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.150
Manager, you take care of Watari.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.810
Okay, everyone, do your best 
and get us to the Inter-High!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.660
<b>Certificate of Merit
Second Place</b>

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:49.520
Right!

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.660
Yah!

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.660
Sure.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:55.000
Uh... "team"? "Understand"?

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.020
Darn it!

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:58.290
A man don't need English to make sasakama!

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:02.580
Sasashichi might expand abroad someday.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.860
Good point!

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:06.390
What's "sasakama" in English?

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.680
I... I don't know.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:13.020
Sa... Sasa...

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:13.020
Endless: without end, 
continuing forever.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.670
Well, that's not going to be on the test...

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:16.860
Finally: at last, in the end.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.400
Onagawa, you memorized vocabulary!

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:23.840
These words all appear 
in Tan-Tan Girls lyrics.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:25.780
Thank you, Ma-chan.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.150
Here it is!

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:29.770
Sasa is "bamboo grass"!

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:32.660
Ma-chan! Ma-chan! Ma-chan!

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.660
Maybe I'll need English some day after all!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.370
<i>I-I'll have yer head!</i>

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.500
<i>Stay back, Matsuo-anego!</i>

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.830
<i>Die! Gragh!</i>

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.770
<i>What gang sent you?!</i>

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:42.380
<i>Shaddup!</i>

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.720
What are you studying now?

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:45.920
Kanji.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.470
<b>INTIMIDATE   DOMINATE   ESCALATE   TERRITORY</b>

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.180
<b>CONFISCATE</b>

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:04.180
"I made a big flag..." Um...

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:05.710
Flutter.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.890
Oh! Th-Thanks.

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:13.650
"...flutter. It was built by the 
sign of the person who..."

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.360
Approached.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:19.040
Wait, Misato-kun, how do you know all this?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.440
I've memorized that part.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:24.580
Misato-kun, you really are per—

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.460
—fect? Don't say that.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.390
Huh? Where is everyone?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.560
Out there.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:44.020
<b>D

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:42.700
Workin' the brain sure makes a man hungry...

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.650
I don't think yours got much of a workout.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.740
How's studying going for you, Shotaro?

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.820
Um...

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.680
Could you make way, Futaba?

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.620
Misato-kun, is that...

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.870
Dinner.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.350
How considerate of you, Misato.

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.050
Rice balls!

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.430
I made plenty. There are more in the kitchen.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.340
Wow, they look great!

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.740
Now this sates my hunger!

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:21.240
Are other teams forbidden from
using the facilities if they fail classes?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.160
Doubt it.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:27.520
I made a promise to the coach when we 
formed the men's rhythmic gymnastics club.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:28.870
That's right.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:32.500
You said something about him 
making a place for you...

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:35.270
Did you mean the team?

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:36.220
Yep!

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:40.290
But the coach was the ace of 
Hakumei University, wasn't he?

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.410
He was indeed a superlative athlete.

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.330
So much so that if he'd stayed in the game,

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:49.550
they say he could've changed the history 
of men's rhythmic gymnastics.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:51.800
<b>Men's
Rhythmic
Gymnastics
Club</b>

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.680
<b>Soshukan High School</b>

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.180
Shusaku.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.050
Shusaku.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.460
Dinner.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.900
Oh, is it that time already?

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.010
Thanks.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.930
Misato-kun made them.

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:19.660
They look great!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.490
You seem absorbed.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:26.920
Yeah, I'm having so much 
fun watching them go.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.990
You've been more like 
your old self lately.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:32.590
What? No way!

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:34.130
Does my face look all intense and mean?

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:39.480
My old self, huh? Can't say I'm a fan...

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:40.780
First-years, gather 'round!

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:41.690
Yes, sir!

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:44.780
We're changing up the practice regime.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:45.570
No way!

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:46.350
I'm dead.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:47.400
What was that?!

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:52.270
<b>GO FOR IT
Unity! Bonding!!</b>

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.110
Y-Yes, sir!

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:51.750
You're wasting your time, Mabuchi-senpai.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:55.650
Competition requires wholehearted devotion.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:59.750
If they can't give you that, 
it doesn't matter what you teach them.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.280
Shida...

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:07.080
And it bugs me to waste time
on these bottom-feeding dregs.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.500
Hey, that's a little much!

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.080
We're doing our best!

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:11.750
Hey!

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.930
Your best, huh?

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.750
If he was that great, why did he quit?

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:27.730
<b>Men's
Rhythmic
Gymnastics
Club Dorm</b>

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.730
I heard he injured himself 
the day before the tournament.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.260
He hid it and competed anyway.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.420
Shida! Shida!

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.530
Why didn't you tell me you were hurt?

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.290
Because the here and now is all that matters.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:51.710
I perform without thought for the future.

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:54.950
I only live in the moment.

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.810
And this is where that got you.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:01.900
I'm going to soar again.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:17.190
<i>You should be able 
to go about your daily life.</i>

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:20.950
<i>But you'll never compete again.</i>

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:26.120
<i>I'd recommend finding a 
profession outside of athletics.</i>

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.750
<i>You're still young, so you have time.</i>

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.480
Damn it...

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:34.580
Damn it.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:43.850
Congratulations on your discharge.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:45.190
Thanks.

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:47.300
What are you going to do now?

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:50.740
Dunno. Guess I'll wander aimlessly here.

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:53.280
Or go back to Japan 
and wander aimlessly there.

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:57.020
I don't have any plans for the future, 
so I guess I'll just do whatever.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.740
Look at you walking!

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.130
You're walking, Shida-san.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:09.380
What does that matter?

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:12.250
You worked hard to be 
on your own two feet again.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.890
If you hadn't put in the effort, 
you wouldn't even be standing here.

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:18.830
Please don't diminish your hard work.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:24.380
It might take you to an even brighter future.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.390
Married?

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.430
Who to?

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.870
Someone she met in Germany.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:34.230
Shusaku Shida, I think?

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.200
She said he used to do 
gymnastics at Shiro University.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.810
Or... was it rhythmic gymnastics?

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:40.790
Huh.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.030
I didn't know men did rhythmic gymnastics.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.830
Apparently they do.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:47.210
Asao, you'll be coming with us to meet him.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.490
What do you want to wear?

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:49.850
Any ideas?

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:52.950
Are you listening, Asao?

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:02.980
Hello, Asao-chan. 
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:07.750
You're different.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.870
You don't do rhythmic gymnastics any more?

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:12.390
Not as an athlete.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:15.560
But I'm thinking of becoming a coach.

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:19.730
Shida? Oh, from Shiro University?

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.530
I've got all the help I need.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.840
We don't have enough members for a team.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:29.250
Sorry, but you'll have to look elsewhere.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:32.740
Jeez, that was Shida-senpai again!

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:38.810
Sorry, but Shiro University and 
Shiro High both have enough help.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.920
If I find anything, I'll let you know.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:44.170
Okay. Thank you.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.710
I appreciate it.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:50.410
I know Mabuchi-senpai asked 
and all, but that guy...

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:53.060
When I think back on
 everything he said to me...

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:57.820
I doubt he wants to work 
for "dregs" like us anyway.

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:03.590
<i>You found a job? Where?</i>

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.070
Ao High.

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.030
Soshukan Private High School!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.830
<i>Does Ao High even have 
a men's rhythmic gymnastics team?</i>

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.160
They don't.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.590
I'll be teaching English and 
advising the newspaper club.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.360
Thank you for all your help.

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:19.230
See you.

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:04.800
Ow, ow, ow...

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.460
Yeah, go figure...

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:07.870
Whoa! Awesome!

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:08.950
That was so cool!

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:10.680
Teach me how to do that!

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:11.700
Me too, me too!

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:13.290
You're like a superhero!

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.720
So cool!

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:20.890
<b>Men's
Rhythmic
Gymnastics
Club Dorm</b>

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:20.890
And that's when he taught you 
to do backflips, right?

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:21.950
Yeah.

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:24.820
Then Tsukidate and Onagawa joined up.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:28.650
When the Inter-High was held in 
Aomori, he took us to see it.

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:32.530
Seeing our first group routine...
That was incredible!

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.040
<b>TSURUYA</b>

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.040
<b>T
A
K
O
Y
A
K
I</b>

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:37.040
Have you all decided which 
high schools you'll attend?

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.030
Actually...

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:43.930
We'd like to go where you teach, Shida-san!

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:47.370
And we'd like to do 
group rhythmic gymnastics!

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:48.460
What?

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:52.400
But Ao High doesn't have a
 men's rhythmic gymnastics team...

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:53.590
Um...

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:55.980
What about a different school?

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.890
I know! Maybe Sendai Tokuou?

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:00.880
If you'd like, we can sit in sometime.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:05.080
Let's just form a team, then. An MRG club.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:09.090
We'll start a men's rhythmic 
gymnastics team at Ao High!

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:10.650
Come on, man...

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.830
Take this seriously.

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.540
But it's the only way!

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.040
Of course...

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.280
Of course! That's just it!

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:21.330
Shida-san?

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.910
I'll make a place for you to belong.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.910
I'll start the men's rhythmic gymnastics club!

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:29.420
Right!

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.130
See? Told ya so!

00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:35.090
Onagawa got us this time.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.690
What? A men's rhythmic gymnastics club?

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:40.790
Yes. I have all the materials.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:42.340
Please give them a look.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.840
I don't know why I didn't realize it sooner.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:50.030
I suppose I still wasn't facing reality.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:53.110
It's the same arrogance 
I felt during my ace days.

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.910
I was so sure that someone 
would reach out to me...

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:59.550
That there was a place I'd be welcomed...

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.370
But that wasn't the case.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:05.530
I needed to make it for myself.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:07.470
Sounds like you're having fun.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:10.470
Head Teacher!

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:12.610
Did you watch the videos I gave you?

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:14.170
Of course not.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.950
Why not?

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.800
There's no need.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:22.100
You can't understand the appeal of men's 
rhythmic gymnastics without watching those!

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.270
What's the point?

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:28.560
I already know a club like that won't bring 
anything worthwhile to our school.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:29.900
Just give up.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.020
Head Teacher!

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:52.750
And real men's rhythmic 
gymnastics is even better.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:57.970
It's five, ten... a hundred times
 more powerful and beautiful!

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.200
Please, at least watch them!

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.640
Watch and decide for yourself!

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.230
Please!

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:06.980
<b>Principal's Office</b>

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:08.330
The copious materials you brought

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:11.730
have shown me the basics 
of men's rhythmic gymnastics.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:14.380
But the dorms are filled with other teams.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:16.620
I'll take a warehouse or a spare room.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.860
You need a specialized mat, don't you?

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.150
We don't have the budget for that.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:25.120
We'll borrow the one at Sekiou University.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:29.120
Oh? You know someone 
who can get you in there?

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.710
Very well.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:39.680
I'll put in a good word 
at Sekiou University for you.

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:43.880
Senpai.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:46.980
Why are you willing to go so far for me?

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.330
You're not a prodigy, you know?

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.360
I know how hard you worked 
to get where you were.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.440
What you felt was genuine.

00:18:57.230 --> 00:19:00.280
Of course, your obnoxiousness 
was the real deal, too.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.820
But I could ask you the same 
question... Why go this far?

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:07.290
With these boys, I think...

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:11.940
I think I can soar again.

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.170
All right!

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.180
<b>Men's
Rhythmic
Gymnastics
Club</b>

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:22.430
We did it!

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:23.500
Yeah!

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:26.060
<b>Sekiou University</b>

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:32.240
This feels pretty great!

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:33.690
Shida-san...

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.390
I mean, Coach!

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:38.380
We'll make a promise, too!

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:41.990
We're gonna take you to the Inter-High!

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:44.720
Sure.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:46.490
We'll all study hard, too!

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.640
We won't fail one subject!

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:53.880
If we do, you can bar us from
 using this gym for a year!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.140
You're sure?

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:57.660
Yes! A man keeps his word!

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:01.110
Then do it, Shichigahama-kun...

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:03.520
Captain!

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:06.640
Yes, sir!

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:09.430
And that's why we can't fail a single test.

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:12.110
I'm going to go study!

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:15.270
I have a question.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.070
What?

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.300
The details of your story just now

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:22.390
suggest it wasn't the coach
 who proposed the deal.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.930
<i>We won't fail one subject!</i>

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:30.120
<i>If we do, you can bar us from
 using this gym for a year!</i>

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.260
You know, come to think of it...

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:41.510
<b>SQUEEZE   SQUEEZE   SQUEEZE   SQUEEZE   SQUEEZE</b>

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:41.510
Don't tell me you're just now 
realizing what you did!

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.510
Shichigahama!

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:44.260
<b>GRIND   GRIND   GRIND   GRIND   GRIND   GRIND   GRIND</b>

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:45.930
This is all your fault!

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:55.810
<b>SHRED   SHRED   SHRED   SHRED   SHRED   SHRED</b>

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:49.120
You'll pay! At long last, you will pay!

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:51.190
That's a relief. Bye.

00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:53.720
Wait! You're leaving, Misato-kun?

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:55.810
After throwing that grenade?!

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.680
I thought something was weird!

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.440
The coach would never make us promise that!

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:00.530
What do you want from me?!

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.940
After all the coach did for us, 
any man would've promised that!

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:06.120
Would not!

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:11.950
<i>But we still worked hard, and in the end...</i>

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:15.000
Coach! We all passed all our tests!

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:18.580
Good. Let's get started, then.

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:19.500
Yes, sir!

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:23.970
<i>We're soaring again today!</i>
